===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# To lose a ninth.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1973|url=https://books.google.ca/books?id=wDZtAAAAMAAJ&q=ninthing|title=Herakles on Thasos|page=79
|passage=οὐ[δ̓] ὲνατεὐεται, should be translated “a tithe (offering or fee) is not given (or paid)”, “no tithing” (literally, “a ninth is not given”, “no '''ninth-ing'''”, if I may coin such a word).}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|url=https://books.google.ca/books?id=25k6DwAAQBAJ&pg=PA161|title=Religion and Reconciliation in Greek Cities: The Sacred Laws of Selinus and Cyrene|page=161
|passage=A yearling "is '''ninthed'''" for Semele on Myconos (LSCG 96.23–24); the victim "is not '''ninthed'''" for Heracles Thasios}}
# To divide by nine.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|url=https://books.google.ca/books?id=KKXiBQAAQBAJ&pg=PA255|title=Contributions to Survey Sampling and Applied Statistics: Papers in Honor of H.O Hartley
|passage=THE NINTHER-MEAN COMBINATION When data are only a little worse than usual, so far as wild and straggling values are concerned, we can do well enough by taking means of the results of '''ninthing'''.}}

